-- title:
--   Actual original BV positive C1 Taylor error vanishes in expectation on sample-dependent stopped physical grids
-- statement:
--   For the authentic original BV Levy X, admissible original D, jump-removed Y and real C1 value function w, prove that the expected positive part of the literal discounted physical Taylor error converges to zero on sample-dependent grids. Assumptions are precisely the original sub-cap C1 value-function smoothness, a common compact positive-subcap band on all stopped cell segments, pathwise shrinking maximal Y grid increments, endpoint consistency and residual a.e. strong measurability; a Lipschitz constant is obtained from the genuine C1 hypothesis rather than added. In particular this theorem supports random stopped physical partitions and invokes true original BV L1 domination, never the circular BV prebudget.
-- source:
--   Integrates original C1 compact derivative/Lipschitz certificate eecd0a2e-94ac-4e1a-8b44-2476caec3569 with fresh sample-dependent-grid positive mean child V. It is the clean adapter for P3-GRID4's exact stopped-grid witness; boundary contact remains independent.

